{% extends 'help/partials/base.html.twig' %}

{% set id = 'Submissions' %}

{% block header %}
    Submitting
{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <p>
        Submit your solution with the green button, either in the navigation menu or next to the problem on the
        Problemset page.
    </p>
    <img src="{{ asset('images/help/submit.png') }}" alt="Submitting"
         class="mb-3 rounded-3 img-fluid help-img">
    <p>
        The solution is sent for automatic checking. You can follow the results on the Scoreboard or on the Team
        page in the Submissions section. Blue means the check is running, green a correct solution, red an incorrect one.
    </p>
    <img src="{{ asset('images/help/submissions.png') }}" alt="Submission results"
         class="mb-3 rounded-3 img-fluid help-img">
    <p>The result can be one of the following:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <b>compiler-error</b>: Your program failed to compile. Open the submission to see the compiler's error messages.
        </li>
        <li>
            <b>timelimit</b>: The program ran longer than the time allowed for this problem, so it was stopped. This can mean
            that your program is stuck in a loop or that your solution is not efficient enough.
        </li>
        <li>
            <b>run-error</b>: An error occurred while your program was running. This can have various causes, for example
            dividing by zero, indexing an array outside its bounds, and so on.
        </li>
        <li>
            <b>memory-limit</b>: The program used more memory than this problem allows, for example because of very large arrays or
            recursion that goes too deep.
        </li>
        <li>
            <b>no-output</b>: The program produced no output.
        </li>
        <li>
            <b>output-limit</b>: Your program produced more output than the limit allows.
        </li>
        <li>
            <b>wrong-answer</b>: Your solution's answer was incorrect. This may simply be a mistake in your solution, but
            the output also has to match the format given in the problem statement exactly.
        </li>
        <li>
            <b>too-late</b>: You did not submit your solution before the contest ended. It is stored but will not be judged.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        Keep in mind that the sample inputs do <span class="font-weight-bold">not</span> contain all the tests the
        solution has to pass.
        If your attempt turns red, it does not mean it was entirely wrong! It may just have failed a particular case.
    </p>
{% endblock %}
